  (2051, '', 'Renault', '5 Turbo', '', 'Majorette', '60th Anniversary Edition Deluxe Cars', '', '', '', 0),
  (1327, '1980', 'Renault', '5 Turbo', '', 'Norev', 'Renault Collection', 'French', 'Retro Hot Hatch', 'The Renault 5 had already been a best-seller for 6 years. No other car would be better placed as the springboard for an ambitious project for Renault, namely to offer the 1st French car with turbocharged petrol engine as standard.', 0),
  (1326, '1982', 'Renault', '5 Turbo 9', '', 'Norev', 'Renault Collection', 'French', 'Retro Rally', 'Driven by Jean Ragnotti in 1981, the 5 Turbo won the Monte Carlo Rally on its first outing in the World Rally Championship.', 0),
  (1328, '1969', 'Renault', '8 Gordini', '', 'Norev', 'Renault Collection', 'French', 'Retro Rally', 'Renault 8 Gordini signalled the dawn of a new sports driving age (or almost). By offering a sporty version - under the name Gordini - of a large series model, Renault could offer affordable sports cars: it was the birth of the GTI before the name even existed.', 0),
